From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RCT Screensaver <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:55:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Title screen: read the next park in the background

While a title sequence plays, a LOAD of a .park file now reads and
decompresses the file and reads the object files it needs on a separate
thread; the current park keeps playing meanwhile. Registering the objects,
importing the park and preparing playback still run on the main thread
once the read is done. Seek() and the first load stay synchronous, and any
failure falls back to the normal path (skip to the next load).

ObjectManager gains PreloadObjects() (thread-safe read of objects that are
not loaded yet) and a LoadObjects() overload that takes them.
